    "body": "This change creates a circular dependency. `logger.ts` now imports `safeInvoke` from `@/lib/backend/core`, but `core.ts` imports `getLogger` from `@/lib/logger`. The dependency chain is: `logger.ts` → `core.ts` → `logger.ts`.\n\nThis is particularly dangerous because the logger is initialized very early in the application lifecycle, and the circular import can cause one of the modules to resolve as `undefined` at load time. In this case, when `logger.ts` is first loaded, it triggers the load of `core.ts`, which tries to call `getLogger` from `logger.ts`—but `logger.ts` hasn't finished evaluating yet.\n\nThe fix is to revert `logger.ts` to use `import { invoke } from '@tauri-apps/api/core'` directly (or to use `@tauri-apps/plugin-log` which the module comment says it's built on top of). `logger.ts` is the lowest-level logging primitive and should not depend on any wrapper that itself depends on the logger.\n```suggestion\nimport { invoke } from '@tauri-apps/api/core';\n```",
