    "body": "The assertion was updated to `expect.anything()`, but the test still mocks `@tauri-apps/api/core` on line 23 and imports `invoke` from `@tauri-apps/api/core` on line 8. Since `AgentSessionListContext.tsx` now uses `safeInvoke` from `@/lib/backend/core`, the old mock at `@tauri-apps/api/core` no longer intercepts calls made by the context. This means:\n1. The mock won't provide controlled return values for `agent_get_all_sessions`, causing real Tauri IPC calls or unhandled errors in the test environment.\n2. The spy assertion `expect(invoke).toHaveBeenCalledWith(...)` will always fail since the wrong function is being tracked.\n\nThe mock block (currently at line 23) needs to be changed to target `@/lib/backend/core` with `safeInvoke` exported as the mock function, and the import/spy variable should be updated to reference `safeInvoke` from `@/lib/backend/core`.",
